{"_data": [{"contents": [{"type": "lesson_name", "content": ""}, {"type": "unit_name", "content": "Life Cycle in ASP.NET"}, {"type": "position", "content": 2}, {"type": "origin", "content": "stub"}, {"type": "lesson", "content": 1}, {"type": "level", "content": "B1.2"}], "type": "metadata"}, {"contents": [{"type": "test", "content": "false"}], "type": "achievment_test"}, {"contents": [{"type": "text", "content": "These are words you hear and use to talk life cycle in ASP.NET."}], "type": "target_word_describer"}, {"contents": [{"type": "primary", "content": "Understand information about web applications, their principles and basic concepts in a range of work contexts.  Describe applications for an operating system for personal computers in a range of work contexts."}, {"type": "secondary_1", "content": "Discusses a range of options for potential actions at work through the correct use of grammar, vocabulary; level of formality and purpose, and cohesion and coherence aspects appropriate to this level.  Exchanges simple information on web applications, and applications for operating systems for personal computers."}], "type": "objectives"}, {"type": "background_image", "content": "enpe7n6le01ob02re1img01.jpg"}, {"contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "embedded "}, {"type": "definition", "content": "when something comes linked to another thing"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(adjective)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: There are three main aspects that are embedded."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "enpe7n6le01ob02aud01"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "assemble"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "to put together parts of something "}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(verb)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: That's my favorite platform to assemble applications."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "enpe7n6le01ob02aud02"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "dynamic "}, {"type": "definition", "content": "that depends on power "}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(adjective)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: ASP.NET life cycle specifies the processes on the ASP.NET pages that produce dynamic output."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "enpe7n6le01ob02aud03"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "cycle "}, {"type": "definition", "content": "a process that repeats actions after they are finished"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(noun)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: ASP.NET life cycle specifies the processes on the ASP.NET pages that produce dynamic output."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "enpe7n6le01ob02aud04"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "directive "}, {"type": "definition", "content": "an instruction which is made authoritatively  "}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(noun)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: There is a page directive which set ups the environment where everyone works."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "enpe7n6le01ob02aud05"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "track "}, {"type": "definition", "content": "to check constantly a progress "}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(verb)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: It tracks pages and put them together in a dynamic way."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "enpe7n6le01ob02aud06"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"type": "heading", "content": "Simple Present Passive in Affirmative"}, {"type": "describer", "content": "We use sentences in <strong>simple present passive</strong> or <strong>present passive voice </strong>when we want to stand out the function of an object in a sentence rather than the subject.   "}, {"type": "text", "content": "When we aim to highlight the person or element that performs an action, we use active voice:  </br></br>  \u2022\t<strong>ASP.NET</strong> processes pages and it produces a dynamic output to specify the life cycle. </br></br>  But when it comes to highlighting the role of the object in a sentence, we need to use the passive voice: </br></br>  \u2022\t<i><strong>Pages </strong> are processed to specify the life cycle.  </br>  \u2022\t<strong>Pages</strong> are processed <strong>by</strong> ASP.NET to specify the life cycle. </i></br> </br>  When using the passive voice the subject could be omitted, but in case you wish to mention it, you need to use the particle <b>by</b> followed by the noun. </br></br>   "}, {"type": "example", "content": "There are three main aspects that are embedded."}, {"type": "example", "content": "On this state, ApplicationManager is created, as well as something called HostingEnvironment which provides information about resources. "}, {"type": "example", "content": "We also have a stage where response objects are created, and another one where objects are assigned to the request; the latter is processed by the HttpApplication class."}, {"type": "text", "content": "This is the grammatical structure we need to use when building sentences in <strong>simple present passive</strong>: </br></br>   <center>Object + <strong>Verb be + Verb in past participle</strong> + Complement</center></br></br>   For example:  </br> </br> \u2022\t<i>Life cycles <strong>are divided</strong>  into applications and pages in ASP.NET.</i>"}], "type": "learning_points"}, {"contents": [{"type": "heading", "content": "ASP.NET Page Life Cycle Events"}, {"type": "describer", "content": "There are a series of <span class=\"strong\">events </span> that appear at each stage of <span class=\"strong\">ASP.NET page life cycle </span>. "}, {"type": "text", "content": "During a life cycle we have some stages that present some events. These events are coded and come with an event handler which is a function or subroutine. <br/> <br/> The following chart includes the event present in an <span class=\"strong\">ASP.NET page life cycle</span>: "}, {"type": "image", "content": "enpe7n6le01ob02img01.jpg"}, {"type": "example", "content": "I know about how ASP.NET processes pages. I also know that it has some stages in the application life cycle."}], "type": "learning_points"}, {"contents": [{"type": "text", "content": "Search for more information about applications life cycle in ASP.NET. "}, {"type": "text", "content": "Identify the stages of an application life cycle and classify the information in order of importance.  "}, {"type": "text", "content": "Create a mind map to explain all the stages of an applications life cycle in ASP.NET.  "}, {"type": "text", "content": "Prepare an oral presentation to explain your mind map. "}, {"type": "text", "content": "Share your work with the class. "}], "type": "takeaway_extension"}, {"contents": [{"type": "text", "content": "I search for information about applications life cycle in ASP. "}, {"type": "text", "content": "I identify and classify the stages of an application life cycle in ASP.NET "}, {"type": "text", "content": "I create a mind map to explain all the stages.  "}, {"type": "text", "content": "I prepare an oral presentation to explain my mind map.  "}, {"type": "text", "content": "I share my work with the class. "}], "type": "takeaway_assessment"}], "type": "sena", "labs": [{"stimuli": [{"template_override": 1, "_data": [], "type": "welcome", "id": 0, "contents": [{}]}, {"template_override": 1, "contents": [{"value": {"images": [{"time": "100", "image": "enpe7n6le01ob02re2img01.jpg", "id": 0, "text": "<span class=\"strong\">Jessica</span>: Hey, could you help me with my homework? I have to prepare a presentation about the ASP.NET life cycle. <br><span class=\"strong\">Nestor</span>: Sure, that's my favorite platform to assemble applications. What do you want to know?<br><span class=\"strong\">Jessica</span>: First, I need to say what the ASP.NET life cycle specifies.<br><span class=\"strong\">Nestor</span>:  That's easy. There are three main aspects that are embedded; first, ASP.NET life cycle specifies the processes on the ASP.NET pages that produce dynamic output. Second, it tells us how applications and pages are processed and instantiated. Finally, it tracks pages and put them together in a dynamic way. <br>"}, {"time": "50000", "image": "enpe7n6le01ob02re2img02.jpg", "id": 1, "text": "<span class=\"strong\">Jessica</span>: Great. Can you tell me about them?<br><span class=\"strong\">Nestor</span>: Of course. First, you request access to an application resource, then the browser sends the request to a web server. After that, the second stage involves a unified pipeline which receives the request. On this state, ApplicationManager is created, as well as something called HostingEnvironment which provides information about resources. We also have a stage where response objects are created, and another one where objects are assigned to the request; the latter is processed by the HttpApplication class.<br>"}, {"time": "92000", "image": "enpe7n6le01ob02re2img03.jpg", "id": 2, "text": "<span class=\"strong\">Jessica</span>: Excellent! One last thing. I am sure I'll have to exemplify my explanation by providing an example in a work context. <br><span class=\"strong\">Nestor</span>:  That's easy; you can tell them to imagine a company that is organized by different departments. Each department manages sensitive data and has control over items that were inherited from management. Just as in ASP.NET, there is a page directive which sets up the environment where everyone works; there is a code selection to establish the events; and finally, a page layout where you can see the final product. <br><span class=\"strong\">Jessica</span>: You're amazing! Thanks for your help!"}], "coverimg": "enpe7n6le01ob02re2img01.jpg", "audiosrc": "enpe7n6le01ob02re2aud01"}, "type": "slideshow"}], "type": "audio", "_data": [], "id": 3, "title": ""}], "exercises": [{"stimuli_ids": [0], "template_override": 1, "questions": [], "type": "WLC", "_data": [{"contents":